{%- comment -%}
  Product names are stored in Title Case ("Nikita Dress") and shown in CAPS.

  Google Merchant Center flags ALL-CAPS titles as "Excessive capitalization",
  and screen readers often spell all-caps words out letter by letter. So the
  DATA is Title Case — which is what Google, Googlebot, admin exports and
  assistive tech read — while CSS does the shouting for human shoppers.
  text-transform is purely visual and never reaches the DOM text.

  The theme already uppercases four surfaces when settings.product_title_uppercase
  is on: .product-card-title, .cart-product-link, .product-add-to-cart-sticky--title
  and .thb-product-detail .product-title.uppercase--true. This block is the
  top-up for the ones it misses — image hotspots, and any .product-title that
  renders outside .thb-product-detail or without the uppercase--true class
  (quick view, product recommendations, drawers, search results).

  Remove this block and turn off the theme setting to show real Title Case.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- if settings.product_title_uppercase -%}
<style id="carbon-uppercase-titles">
  .product-title-uppercase-true .product-title,
  .product-title-uppercase-true .product-card-title,
  .product-title-uppercase-true .cart-product-link,
  .product-title-uppercase-true .thb-hotspot-product-title,
  .product-title-uppercase-true .product-recommendations .product-title,
  .product-title-uppercase-true .predictive-search .product-title {
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  /* carbon-uppercase-breadcrumbs */
  .product-title-uppercase-true .breadcrumbs {
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>
{%- endif -%}

